hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15375","Haddathana Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Taymi, meaning Sulayman, from Abu Uthman, meaning al-Nahdi, from Amir ibn Malik, from Safwan ibn Umayyah, he said: Plague, belly, drowning, and childbirth are martyrdom. Abu Uthman related it to us many times, and he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once."
"15376","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Sharik informed us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rafi', from Umayyah ibn Safwan ibn Umayyah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed armor from him on the day of Khaybar, and he said: Seizure, O Muhammad? He said: Rather a guaranteed loan. He said: Some of it was lost, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered to guarantee it for him, and he said: Today, O Messenger of Allah, I am more desirous of Islam."
"15377","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah, haddathana al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abd Allah ibn Safwan, from his father, that Safwan ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf was told: Whoever did not emigrate has perished. He said: So I said: I will not reach my family until I come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I rode my mount and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, they claim whoever did not emigrate has perished. He said: No, O Abu Wahb; return to the valleys of Makkah. He said: While I was sleeping, a thief came and took my garment from under my head, so I caught him and brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This one stole my garment. So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that he be cut. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is not what I wanted; it is charity upon him. He said: Why not before you brought him to me?"
"15378","Haddathana Zakariya ibn Adi, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Safwan ibn Umayyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave to me on the day of Hunayn when he was the most hateful of people to me, and he kept giving me until he became the most beloved of people to me."
"15379","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ja'far, haddathana Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Tariq ibn Muraqqa', from Safwan ibn Umayyah, that a man stole his cloak and he raised him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who commanded his cutting. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have pardoned him. He said: Why was this not before you brought him to me, O Abu Wahb? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut him."
"15380","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Wuhayb, haddathana Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Safwan ibn Umayyah, that it was said to him: None enters Paradise except who emigrated. He said: So I said: I will not enter my house until I come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this one stole a khamisah of mine with a man accompanying him, and he commanded his cutting. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have granted it to him. He said: Why not before you brought him to me? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, they say none enters Paradise except who emigrated. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no emigration after the conquest of Makkah, but jihad and intention; when you are called to march, then march."
"15381","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, informed us, from Abu Uthman, meaning al-Nahdi, from Amir, meaning Ibn Malik, from Safwan ibn Umayyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Plague is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, belly is martyrdom, and childbirth is martyrdom."
"15382","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Adi, from Sulayman, from Abu Uthman, from Amir ibn Malik, from Safwan ibn Umayyah, he said: Plague, belly, drowning, and childbirth are martyrdom. Sulayman said: Abu Uthman related it to us, meaning many times, and he raised it once to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15383","Haddathana Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, he said: Safwan ibn Umayyah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me taking meat from the bone with my hand and said: O Safwan. I said: At your service. He said: Bring the meat near your mouth, for it is more wholesome and more pleasant."
"15384","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad, haddathana Sulayman, meaning Ibn Qarm, from Simak, from Humayd the nephew of Safwan ibn Umayyah, from Safwan ibn Umayyah, he said: I was sleeping in the mosque upon a khamisah of mine, and it was stolen; we seized the thief and raised him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who commanded his cutting. I said: O Messenger of Allah, for a khamisah worth thirty dirhams? I grant it to him or sell it to him. He said: Why was it not before you brought him to me?"
